re Names]" /></encodings></pane></panes><rows>[federated.complexity].[sum:sla_pct:qk] + [federated.complexity].[sum:reassigned_pct:qk]</rows><cols>[federated.complexity].[none:Complexity_Band:nk]</cols></table></worksheet></worksheets><dashboards><dashboard name="Case Assignment Fairness and SLA Control Tower"><style /><size maxheight="3200" maxwidth="1400" minheight="3200" minwidth="1400" /><zones><zone h="100000" id="1" type-v2="layout-basic" w="100000" x="0" y="0"><zone h="100000" id="2" param="vert" type-v2="layout-flow" w="100000" x="0" y="0"><zone h="6000" id="3" type-v2="text" w="100000" x="0" y="0"><formatted-text><run fontsize="18" bold="true">Case Assignment Fairness and SLA Control Tower</run><run fontsize="9">
ClearPath Case Services (fictional) · 15,908 cases · 2 January to 30 June 2026. Leadership asked which team was underperforming. Workload per analyst hour is near-equal across all five teams, yet SLA compliance ranges from 26% to 84%. The cause is a target and a routing method, not a team.</run></formatted-text></zone><zone h="23500" id="4" name="SLA compliance by case type, against its own target" w="100000" x="0" y="6000" /><zone h="23500" id="5" name="Routing accuracy by method" w="100000" x="0" y="29500" /><zone h="23500" id="6" name="What a reassignment costs" w="100000" x="0" y="53000" /><zone h="23500" id="7" name="Does the complexity score predict anything?" w="100000" x="0" y="76500" /></zone></zone></zones></dashboard></dashboards></workbook>